XLSX pivot tables keep Excel's header and grand total words

Excel's compact pivot shows rowHeaderCaption and colHeaderCaption in
its header cells, "Row Labels" and "Column Labels" by default, and
grandTotalCaption, "Grand Total" by default, on its totals. The import
read these captions and dropped them, so Calc wrote the field names
and "Total Result" over Excel's cells and every save changed the
table's text (Ely R15.11d). The import now keeps each caption, an
empty one too, or Excel's default when the file has none; a compact
table writes them in its header cells, a tabular one still shows
field names. With no row field but the data layout one, the
column fields' own layout decides.
Export writes a caption only when it differs from Excel's default, so
Excel in another language still shows its own words.
